PATIENT DATA AND PRIVACY

This project processes personal data on behalf of a dental practice and must be
assessed against applicable privacy law (including GDPR where it applies) before
any change to data collection or handling. Three constraints follow from the
current implementation and are part of the terms of use for this code:

1. The appointment enquiry form (src/components/sections/contact/
   ContactForm.tsx) does not transmit data to any server. It composes a
   message in the visitor's own mail client via a `mailto:` link. No personal
   data is received, stored, logged, or processed by the site operator as a
   consequence of using it. Any change that introduces server-side
   transmission, storage, or logging of enquiry data alters the privacy
   posture materially and requires a documented lawful basis.
2. The site sets no cookies, and uses no analytics, tag managers, session
   storage, or third-party tracking scripts. This is load-bearing: the absence
   of non-essential cookies is what allows the site to serve without a cookie
   consent banner. Introducing any analytics or tag-manager SDK requires a
   consent mechanism, a privacy policy, and an update to this section.
3. Published reviews carry only a first name and a neighbourhood
   (src/content/site.ts). This is deliberately reduced detail and must not be
   expanded to surnames, full addresses, dates of treatment, or any other
   attribute that would make a patient identifiable — a dental practice's
   readership makes such combinations identifying in a small locality.

Real patient photography, clinical before/after imagery, and case detail must
only be published with documented written patient consent, held on file and
revisitable, specifying the scope of use. The images currently in
public/images/ are generated placeholders and are not real patient records.

